<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yarim-Lim of Alalakh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yarim-Lim was a prince of Yamhad and brother of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abba-el-i">Abba-El I</a>, who in the 18th century BCE received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh</a> and founded a dependent dynasty ruling the kingdom of Mukish under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. His palace at Alalakh was excavated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonard-woolley">Leonard Woolley</a>, and his descendants ruled until the city's destruction in the 16th century BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yarim-lim-of-alalakh.jpg" alt="Yarim-Lim of Alalakh" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nevit Dilmen · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antakya_Arkeoloji_Muzesi_1250344_nevit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
